## PWA — Progressive Web App

The site is configured as a PWA, enabling:

- **Offline support** — previously visited pages are served from cache when offline
- **Home screen installation** — visitors can install the site as an app on Android/iOS
- **Performance** — static assets (CSS, JS, fonts, images) are served from cache on repeat visits
- **Branded browser chrome** — address bar matches the site's brand purple on mobile

### Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `static/sw.js` | Service worker — caching strategies and offline fallback |
| `static/manifest.json` | PWA manifest — name, icons, colours, display mode |
| `static/offline/index.html` | Offline fallback page shown when no connection |
| `static/images/icon-192.png` | PWA home screen icon (192×192) |
| `static/images/icon-512.png` | PWA home screen icon (512×512) |

### Caching strategy

| Asset type | Strategy | Notes |
|------------|----------|-------|
| HTML pages | Network-first | Always tries network, falls back to cached version |
| CSS / JS / fonts | Cache-first | Served from cache, updated in background |
| Images | Cache-first | Cached on first visit |
| Netlify Functions | Bypassed | Never cached — always live |

### Registration

The service worker is registered in the site `<head>`:

```html
<link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#20123a">
```

And in the site scripts:
```javascript
if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) {
    navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js');
}
```

### Updating the cache

Increment `VERSION` in `sw.js` when deploying significant changes — this busts all caches and forces fresh downloads:

```javascript
const VERSION = 'v2'; // ← bump this
```

### Icons

Generated from `eliphant.tif` (white background, dark gray elephant). To regenerate:

```bash
python3 scripts/generate-icons.py
```